			<div class="content" id="post-content-4188565">
									

<p>So, I think the concept is clever. I like the way this plays with language - however I think that by setting the SCP article <em>after</em> the Foundation has figured out how to deal with it limits the story immensely. Like, I would've loved to see the foundation flounder for a bit as they try to think of how the hell to deal with this thing. But instead what you have here is pretty purely concept, but the concept itself does not have much of a sense of escalation. Like, there's a change between part 1 and part 2, but it doesn't feel like a noticeable escalation, if that makes sense.</p>
